  "title": "Research | Mathis Certenais",
  "description": "PhD research on scientific data logistics: modelling, optimising and governing cross-facility workflows across national supercomputers and research storage, grounded in radio astronomy.",
  "aiSummary": "The thesis, “Collaborative System of Systems for Scientific Data Logistics”, treats governance and security as constraints of the same rank as capacity and cost. It sets out five perspectives — modelling, multi-criteria optimisation, sovereignty, provenance and usability — and tests them on the DDF Pipeline, whose runtime fell from 68.8 hours on one node to 8.7 hours on 24.",
